/F1 9.5 Tf
13.2999999999999989 TL
0.118 0.157 0.196 rg
70.8661417322834666 739.8427559055118081 Td
(The Dhargad River watershed is a tributary watershed of the Jaigan River which finally joins the Saryu River) Tj
T* (at Lweta village \(elevation 716m, 29°42'13.551"N Lat and 79°53'40.896"E Long\) in the Bageshwar district of) Tj
T* (Kumaun Himalaya. It represents a classic case of rainfed Himalayan catchments undergoing acute) Tj
T* (hydrological degradation.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (Consequences of Inaction:) Tj
T* (• Water Scarcity: Severe shortages of drinking water during 2-3 peak summer months for human settlements) Tj
T* (and livestock.) Tj
T* (• Ecosystem Degradation: Drying of aquatic biodiversity, loss of soil moisture, and abandonment of terraced) Tj
T* (agriculture.) Tj
T* (• Climate Vulnerability: Increased cloudburst runoff velocities causing rill and gully erosion without) Tj
T* (groundwater infiltration.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (3.0 ABOUT THE DHARGAD RIVER WATERSHED) Tj
T* (The entire Dhargad watershed encompasses an area of 2.32 km² lying between 29°43'38.117"N to) Tj
T* (29°44'53.908"N Latitude and 79°43'39.756"E to 79°44'47.547"E Longitude. The altitude varies from 1,295 m) Tj
T* (to 1,492 m MSL. It is composed of the Raut Gara Formation \(Damta Group\) characterized by quartzites) Tj
T* (interbedded with silky phyllites and slates.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (Phase-I focuses on the experimental recharge zone of Village Jatha and Pass covering 0.17 km² \(17) Tj
T* (hectares\).) Tj
ET
endstream
