(• Infiltration Holes: 10-15 cm depth, 5 cm diameter, density 5 holes/m² constructed with steel bars in) Tj
T* (barren/abandoned fields to catch high-intensity rain drops.) Tj
T* (• Infiltration Trenches: Staggered cuts of 1.0m × 0.5m × 0.3m spaced 5-10m apart on convex hill slopes to break) Tj
T* (sheetwash runoff and force deep percolation into bedrock fissures.) Tj
T* (• Bio-Plugs & Gully Plugs: Constructed with pine needles, local logs, and stones across first-order ephemeral rills) Tj
T* (to arrest velocity and trap sediment.) Tj
T* (• Terrace Ponds: 10-20 m² area, 1-2 m depth shallow retention ponds with earthen embankments constructed in) Tj
T* (association with villagers.) Tj
